C. LAST-10 and SEASONAL
========================================================================================
   last-10-on-surface: both recipes take the 10 matches immediately before this one,
   so they are identical BY CONSTRUCTION (no date anchor involved). Verified:
      592201 rows compared, max |diff| 0.00e+00
   min_periods DOES differ: backtest t10_win needs 4 prior matches (mn=4), live
   tmean(gdf.won, 10, 3) needs 3 -- so live prices some rows the backtest left NaN.

   seasonal (calendar-year expanding, shifted): first match of each player-year has
   no season history at all -- 2.7% of all rows, and 12.7% have fewer than 5.
   Both recipes agree (live yr = this calendar year, strictly before today; backtest
   expanding().mean().shift(1) within the year), so the seasonal block is consistent --
   but it is a JANUARY-RESET window, thin for everyone early in each season.
